 151: #### REQ-002: NGO Organization Profile + Founder Vetting (verification machinery deferred to v1.5 â€” decision-29/r3)
 152: 
 153: NGOs sign up (email-verified) and complete an org profile. In v1, trust is the founder's hand, recorded properly. The self-serve verification pipeline â€” doc upload UI, pending-review queue, document viewer, public badge â€” is deferred to v1.5, because vetting already happens in concierge onboarding: the founder talks to every pilot NGO before admitting it. Two trust tiers in v1; the KYC tier stays v1.5.
 154: 
 155: 1. **Unverified** â€” an email-verified account (the bot floor for any Discovery message). Can draft projects and run Discovery within a 10-credit/day free allowance. When the day's credits run out, it can fund the project's fuel to continue now, or wait for tomorrow's refill. Cannot publish to volunteers.
 156: 2. **Vetted** â€” set by ONE audited admin action during concierge onboarding. The daily free allowance rises to 30/day (the 3Ã— reward). Can publish and fund fuel. This is the default tier for admitted pilot NGOs.
 157: 
 158: - The NGO admin can create and edit the org profile (name, mission, country, website, logo).
 159: - Email verification is required before any Discovery message; the composer is disabled with a verify CTA until confirmed. Vetting remains the publish wall, never the Discovery wall (decision-8).
 160: - **The vetted action is audited (a decision-29/r3 guard):** vetted_by, vetted_at, NGO legal/display name, public reference link, contact name + title + authority attestation (decision-28/s2), evidence type, and a vetting note; an unvet/revoke action exists. Marking vetted or unvetted emits the verification-outcome notification (REQ-016) through the normal event path, so the NGO learns publish is unlocked.
 161: - **Evidence rule (PII-minimizing):** prefer public evidence â€” a registry entry, the website, an EIN lookup. If a registration document must be requested (by email), only its metadata is recorded in-platform and the copy is deleted after vetting. No sensitive personal identity documents in v1.
 162: - **No public "verified" claim in v1.** The flag is internal (or displayed as "founder-vetted"); a document-verified badge returns with the v1.5 pipeline. Nothing implies a document review that did not run.
 163: - On vetting, the daily allowance rises 10 â†’ 30 immediately and for every later day; re-vetting never re-raises (idempotent).
 164: - Only vetted NGOs can publish. An unvetted NGO may reach `scoped`, with Publish disabled ("your ai4good contact completes vetting during onboarding").
 165: - Daily drip (decision-11): the free allowance hard-resets to the tier grant once per UTC day, with no rollover. The daily wall is the deliberate fund-now-or-return-tomorrow moment, and this one mechanism replaces a separate daily message cap.
 166: - **v1.5 gate (explicit):** self-serve doc upload, the review queue + viewer, badge display, and the KYC tier all return before ANY non-concierge admission path opens (organic NGO signup, EU/UK signup). A paid "Discovery wallet" stays excluded in v1 AND v1.5 (decision-8).
