 783: ### v1 MVP (public beta launch)
 784: 
 785: **Decision summary (2026-06-03 pivot + decisions 8â€“22; where entries conflict, the later decision wins):**
 786: - **Pivot (2026-06-03)** â€” The deliverable is a deployed, NGO-self-maintainable tool, not a repo; Track A (NGO maintains via chat; Lovable is the build vehicle and durable home), with Discovery classifying the track. Data governance by disclosure: Discovery records data-sensitivity tiers; the highest tier is fixtures-only-during-build; triage enforces. No cash-out: fuel is non-cash, project-scoped credit (stays on the project; donate or keep) â€” removes payout, cash-refund, and money-transmission rails. Nonprofit entity + blended economics; a real Terms of Service. Concierge-first launch. New v1 REQs: REQ-027 (abandonment/rematch), REQ-029 (observability), REQ-030 (ops/incident + admin money-correction), REQ-031 (content moderation/takedown/secret-scanning).
 787: - **8 â€” Unified fuel + free Discovery allowance.** NGOs and volunteers both consume project fuel; funding is allowed from draft onward; Discovery is free up to a per-NGO daily credit allowance (10/day unverified, 30/day verified). Email verification is the floor for any Discovery message; org-document verification is the wall for publishing to volunteers. First funding and first match acceptance each trigger their own hard acknowledgment. No paid Discovery wallet in v1 or v1.5.
 788: - **9 â€” Git-as-truth PM tree.** Reversed by decision-20; retained only as decision trail.
 789: - **10 â€” Capability-preserving build trim.** Six reshapes of implementation shape with every v1 requirement intact; deferred to v1.5: concierge supply-funnel CRM + hand-match tool (first cohort matched manually), rate-limiting infrastructure, gradual-rollout tooling, analytics dashboard, report/takedown UI, multi-jurisdiction tax registration, self-serve data-erasure UI (manual runbook kept).
 790: - **11 â€” Two-layer money.** Funded fuel stays dollar-pegged (15% skim unchanged; no subscription). The free pre-fuel Discovery phase uses an abstract, context-weighted credit: long conversations and uploaded reference files (REQ-032) cost more, cached content costs less, and output regenerations and system-error retries are free. The allowance is a daily drip with no rollover; verification triples it (10 â†’ 30/day). Transparency: a credit gauge, per-turn cost display, and a cost estimate shown before a file is ingested â€” credits are a free grant, never silently removed (a free grant also carries no stored-value/escheatment exposure). Funding a project flips its Discovery to dollar-metered fuel automatically; the free pool serves only unfunded projects (credits are NGO-bound, fuel is project-bound). At daily exhaustion the NGO can verify, fund to continue now, or return tomorrow â€” the UI says "keep going now," never "go faster."
 791: - **12 â€” Post-Discovery NGO project assistant (REQ-033, new in v1).** A funded project unlocks an ongoing, fuel-metered, read-only NGOâ†”AI assistant that answers "how is my project going?" from tasks, blockers, fuel runway, and recent activity. It never mutates tasks, approves handoff, or accepts scope (changes route through Change Requests). No free credits â€” it disables at fuel zero with a top-up prompt. Proactive/push agents v1.5.
 792: - **13 â€” Opus for Discovery + the assistant.** Discovery is the highest-leverage reasoning step â€” its scope drives the whole build â€” so the strongest model de-risks every downstream volunteer hour. Cost is bounded: Discovery is short and one-time, the daily allowance caps worst-case spend, and the credit unit is model-agnostic so allowances stay 10/30 (the per-credit subsidy is deliberate acquisition spend). The funded assistant's cost passes through to the NGO.
 793: - **14 â€” Automated spend-anomaly engine deferred to v1.5.** The loss ceiling holds without it: no cash-out, first-fund cap, spend caps, fuel-zero cutoff, and a manual rotate-key action mean a leaked key only ever buys bounded compute. The engine only reduced detection latency, which does not bind at pilot scale with daily founder review. Reinstate before organic/EU signup.
 794: - **15 â€” Project comms trimmed to a comment thread.** v1 keeps one project-level comment thread; the full channel (real-time, threads, @-mentions, search) is v1.5. System events go to the notifications and activity feeds, not chat; CR Accept/Decline surfaces on the CR row on the project page.
 795: - **16 â€” Change-Request anti-distraction guardrails** *(surface deferred to v1.5 by 29/r1; the principle governs the v1 informal protocol)*. Volunteer churn is the #1 supply risk, so CRs are opt-in and never interrupt: a low-tone notification with no per-CR email, and only Accept creates work. One open CR per project at a time; Decline is penalty-free and the protected default; the NGO sees expectation-setting framing at submission ("optional; the volunteer decides; adds scope, time, and fuel").
 796: - **17 â€” `paused` state removed from v1.** At pilot scale a pause is a support conversation: pre-match the NGO unpublishes or cancels; mid-build an admin turns off access and leaves a note, or the project is cancelled. Pause/resume returns in v1.5 on the first real request.
